// Form C := alpha*A*B + beta*C,
// A is NIxNK, B is NKxNJ, C is NIxNJ
//
// Optimizations vs. the baseline kernel:
//   - Block the computation along the j (column) dimension using
//     noarr::into_blocks_dynamic so that we work on column tiles of C and B.
//     This improves cache locality for C and B and helps vectorization.
//   - Within each (i, J)-tile and for each k, load A[i, k] only once
