// Form C := alpha*A*B + beta*C,
// A is NIxNK, B is NKxNJ, C is NIxNJ
//
// Compared to the original kernel, this version:
//   - keeps all iteration expressed via Noarr traversers,
//   - keeps the scaling C *= beta separate but still within the traverser,
//   - restructures the multiply-add phase to reuse A[i,k] across the full
